title: "BiDi Coherence-Delta Calculus"
message: "If you use this calculus, reference implementation, or paper source, please cite this repository."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Ellis
    given-names: Edward
date-released: "2026-08-07"
version: "0.3.0"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ETEllis/bidi-coherence-delta-calculus"
abstract: >-
  BiDi Coherence-Delta Calculus is a compact executable substrate for hybrid
  systems with continuous phase flow, guarded balanced-ternary commits, nested
  reference frames, trace/window measurement, and receipt-bound effects.
  Version 0.3.0 adds the guarded Universal Operator and a variational U2 layer
  that differentiates the executed native path, verifies full or explicit
  relative recurrence before constructing monodromy, and emits characteristic
  multipliers only when that gate passes. Finite Lean and Rocq mirrors cover the
  exact carrier, event-order, fixed-aperture, cone-role, sheet-parity, and
  prefix-barrier statements named by the release; runtime covariance and richer
  continuous or physical interpretations remain open.
